-- title:
--   Twisted Brin–Thompson groups of two-transitive actions are finitely presented (case of Zaremsky's Theorem 2.3, OpenAI Boone–Higman)
-- statement:
--   The finite-presentation half of the paper's Theorem 2.3 (Zaremsky), as OpenAI formalized it for the case the paper applies: a faithful action with one orbit on pairs of distinct points. It is an intermediate statement of the split of OpenAI's proof of `OAI.FiniteAlgebraicEnvelopes.main` (the paper's Theorem 1.1, the Boone–Higman equivalence). The paper's Theorem 2.3 assumes less: finitely many orbits on unordered pairs, and a countable nonempty set. That general form is the mission's `theorem_2_3_zaremsky`, which this statement does not prove.
--
--   **Notation** (definitions bundle `OAIFAE003` of this split). For a group $\Gamma$ acting on a set $X$, `Cube X` is $X \to$ (infinite binary sequences), and `TwistedBrinThompson.group` is the subgroup of permutations of `Cube X` generated by the permutations given by a finite table: finitely many source and target dyadic bricks (finitely many coordinates each fixed to a finite binary prefix), with each brick partition covering the cube exactly once, and each source brick mapped onto its target brick by a prefix replacement followed by the coordinate permutation of one element of $\Gamma$.
--
--   **The statement.** Let $\Gamma$ be finitely presented and act faithfully on an infinite set $X$. Suppose that any two distinct points of $X$ can be moved to any two distinct points by one element of $\Gamma$, and that every point stabilizer is finitely generated. Then `TwistedBrinThompson.group` for this action is finitely presented.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Finite algebraic envelopes and the Boone–Higman conjecture, OpenAI Math Release, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (result family 250; paper: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Finite-algebraic-envelopes-and-the-Boone-Higman-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf, Theorem 2.3; Apache License 2.0); Lean: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/GroupTheory/BooneHigman/Main.lean (declaration OAI.FiniteAlgebraicEnvelopes.TwistedBrinThompson.finitelyPresented)

